am2Strata is a new edition of PolyStrata (https://github.com/VecSzn/PolyStrata); parts of it are derived from
PolyStrata's code and web app (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors).

Bundled third-party files keep their own licenses:
- web/vendor/mermaid.min.js: Mermaid 11.4.1, MIT (web/vendor/LICENSE-mermaid.txt)
- web/fonts: the Outfit font, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (web/fonts/OFL.txt)
- poppler/ (the Windows download only): Poppler's pdftotext and pdftoppm, GPL-2.0-or-later, run as separate
  programs to read PDFs (poppler/README.txt says where their source is)

The media engine (crates/strata-media, built only on request) links, through mold (MIT):
- OpenH264 (BSD-2-Clause, Cisco) for MP4 / H.264 video output;
- the Fraunhofer FDK AAC codec (fdk-aac crate; "Software License for The Fraunhofer FDK AAC Codec Library for
  Android", a permissive licence with patent and naming conditions - not OSI-approved) for audio tracks in MP4 files.
- Whisper's mel filter banks from candle's whisper example (MIT or Apache-2.0), crates/strata-media/assets.

With the `onnx` feature, it also uses:
- ort (MIT or Apache-2.0, pyke.io), and ONNX Runtime (MIT, Microsoft), which is loaded at run time and not bundled;
- Chatterbox's text preparation and sampling, ported from resemble-ai/chatterbox (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Resemble
  AI), whose ONNX exports it runs. The weights are downloaded from Hugging Face on request and are not bundled.

It also carries, ported to Rust (crates/strata-media/src/acestep, parler_hf.rs):
- ACE-Step 1.5's model code (MIT, Copyright (c) ACE Studio and StepFun): the song model's condition encoder, diffusion
  transformer, sampler and DCW correction; and Stable Audio's Oobleck decoder as diffusers implements it
  (Apache-2.0, The HuggingFace Team). The weights (ACE-Step/Ace-Step1.5, MIT) are downloaded on request.
- The loading of Parler-TTS mini multilingual v1.1 (Apache-2.0, Hugging Face) and Indic Parler-TTS (Apache-2.0,
  AI4Bharat) into candle's Parler model; their weights and Flan-T5's tokenizer (Apache-2.0, Google) are downloaded on
  request.
